{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>What the gazam left</b> — it came first. Yefet said: for גזם is like גוזז (cutting), and the mem is like the mem in חנם ריקם (gratis, empty). And ילק (yeleq), according to its language, he translated כורת (cutting), and חסיל is like יחסלנו (he will finish it off)."], :book :joel, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "Yefet is the Karaite exegete Yefet ben Eli; the Hebrew incorporates his Arabic glosses. The verbs cited as comparanda (גוזז, יחסלנו) are implicitly cited from other verses."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Joel -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/yoel"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:06:22.922146963Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}